pbus (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The daemon no longer reads a spooled payload where its emitter left it:
    the file is moved into /run/pbus/stage, which only root may write, before
    being checked and read, closing a race where a symbolic link could be put
    in its place between the two. A hard link is refused on its link count.
  * max_payload in pbus.conf, 1 MiB by default, bounds what the daemon reads.
    A payload over 100000 bytes is no longer put in the environment, where it
    made execve fail and stopped the command from running at all; standard
    input carries it and PBUS_PAYLOAD_SIZE is always set.
  * Events can declare payload_pattern, an extended regular expression the
    payload must match; the daemon refuses anything else before a listener
    runs and "pbus emit" exits 6. Documented alongside the quoting rule a
    listener has to follow, since the payload is chosen by the emitter.
  * A listener must now name the account it runs as. "register-listener"
    refuses without -u and pbusd refuses a listener whose file has no user=:
    an absent one used to mean root. Add user=root to restore the previous
    behaviour; postinst names the listeners concerned on upgrade.
  * pbusd no longer inserts a setpriv hop when the listener's user is already
    the one it runs as, and no longer claims "not running as root" when a
    user= names its own account.
  * First release: named-pipe dispatcher daemon, CLI and interactive session,
    listeners as files under /etc/pbus, per-event keys, systemd unit started
    at boot.

 -- pdulvp <pdulvp@laposte.net>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0100
